* The trivial-regime bound on the truncated Perron kernel, ` C <_ T `: the kernel line is split at heights ` -u C ` and ` C ` ( ~ lintsplit ), the middle third is at most ` 2 U ^c C ` ( ~ vedgbnd ) and each tail at most ` U ^c C log ( T / C ) ` ( ~ pkvlog , ~ pkvlogn ).  This is ` norm_perronKernel_le ` of Route Z's PerronKernel.lean, times ` 2 _pi `.

